course: dictionary
lesson: 7697
title: Provide: give what is needed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Provide is a verb. It means to give someone something they need or want. «The school provides lunch for every child.» The clue is that the school gives lunch, so provide means to give what is needed. Try swapping in give: «The school gives lunch for every child» still makes sense, so give is a good meaning.
explain: Provide has useful partners. Provide for means to give someone money, food and a home, as in «Parents provide for their children.» Provide with means to supply something, as in «The office can provide you with a pencil.» Watch the little word after provide, because it changes the meaning.
explain: Provided (that) and providing mean only if. «You can go outside, provided that you finish your work.» The word is not about giving at all. It sets a condition: you may go only if you finish your work. Ask yourself, is this word giving something, or is it setting a rule?
fact: Provide means to give someone something they need or want.
fact: Provide for means to give someone money, food and a home.
fact: «Provided that» and «providing» mean only if.
fact: «A server is a computer that provides a service, such as web pages, videos or a game world.»
fact: In maths, «each box provides 6 eggs» means each box gives you 6 eggs.
exercise: «If you forget your lunch, the school can provide something to eat.» What does provide mean here? | To hide something away | To throw something away | *To give something needed | To count something slowly
exercise: «Each box provides 6 eggs.» How many eggs does one box provide? | 60 | *6 | 16 | 1
exercise: «You can go to the park, provided that you finish your work.» What does provided that mean? | Always | Even though | Because | *Only if
test: «Parents provide for their children by giving them food and a home.» What does provide for mean here? | To paint a picture | To lose a game | To hurry down the road | *To give money, food and a home
test: «A server is a computer that provides a service, such as web pages or videos.» What does a server do? | Sends pencils home | Asks for web pages | *Gives a service, such as web pages or videos | Eats lunch in the hall
exam: «We will go outdoors, providing the rain stops.» What does providing mean here? | Giving out food | Forever | *Only if | Pulling along
